# A02 – Recent Advancements and Future Trends in AI

## Overview
This assignment helped me build a strong foundation in understanding how quickly artificial intelligence is evolving and how those advancements are being applied in real-world industries. It focused on connecting core AI concepts to practical use cases, while also introducing important legal and ethical considerations.

## What I Worked On
In this assignment, I explored several major areas of AI development, including generative models, machine learning, natural language processing, and computer vision. I also looked at how AI is currently being used across industries like healthcare, automotive systems, supply chain management, and smart cities.

One part that stood out to me was learning about different types of generative models like GANs, transformers, and diffusion models. Understanding how models like GPT are built on transformer architecture helped me connect what we learn in class to real tools being used today.

I also compared AI regulations between the European Union and Australia, which helped me understand how different regions approach AI governance. The EU focuses more on strict regulation and accountability, while Australia takes a more flexible, innovation-focused approach.

## What I Learned
This assignment helped me realize that AI is not just about building models, but also about understanding the impact those systems have on society. I learned how advancements in AI are improving industries, but also creating challenges around bias, privacy, and transparency.

It also helped me understand how AI systems are becoming more advanced through multimodal capabilities, meaning they can work with text, images, and audio together. This is important for the future of AI applications.

## Why It Matters
AI is becoming a core part of many industries, and understanding both the technology and its impact is important for building responsible systems. This assignment showed me that future AI development will require a balance between innovation and regulation.
